    "length_0_alt": "Neutral patterned curtains ending in a clean line beside a timber floor",
    "length_0_credit": "Prestigious Textiles · Representative floor relationship",
    "length_0_title": "A clean ending.",
    "length_0_body": "A clear floor relationship keeps the outline composed. Give doors, walkways and everyday movement the space they need.",
    "length_0_look": "Look at the line where fabric meets floor.",
    "length_1_alt": "Patterned curtains with fabric gently resting at the floor",
    "length_1_credit": "Prestigious Textiles · Representative soft break",
    "length_1_title": "A softer ending.",
    "length_1_body": "Fabric gently meeting the floor brings a more relaxed character. Check that the intended finished drop suits your fabric and room.",
    "length_1_look": "Discuss a floor break with the team before ordering; this is not an additional Builder option.",
    "length_note": "Your finished drop remains a measurement, not a style preset. This guide adds no new length specification or puddling option.",
    "position_kicker": "05 / POSITION",
    "position_title_html": "How should the fabric<br>frame the room?",
    "position_intro": "Let the architecture guide the line. Position changes the relationship between fabric, opening and the room beyond.",
    "position_controls": "Compare position",
    "position_0_label": "Window-led",
    "position_1_label": "Ceiling-led",
    "position_0_alt": "Curtains following a tall window and its architectural surround",
    "position_0_credit": "Prestigious Textiles · Window-led example",
    "position_0_title": "Frame the opening.",
    "position_0_body": "A line close to the window keeps attention on its shape and detail. The fabric reads as a frame around the view.",
    "position_0_look": "Notice how the curtain sits in relation to the window surround.",
    "position_1_alt": "A ceiling-mounted TrackFit curtain track extending beyond a window opening",
    "position_1_credit": "TrackFit project · Ceiling-led example",
    "position_1_title": "Give the room a longer line.",
    "position_1_body": "A higher line can emphasise height. Extending beyond the opening can give drawn-back fabric more room and leave more of the view visible.",
    "position_1_look": "Notice the ceiling line and the space beside the opening.",
    "position_note": "These are interior relationships, not fitting instructions. The right position depends on your room, obstructions and suitable fixings.",
    "return_kicker": "06 / RETURN TO FABRIC",
    "return_title_html": "Now find the fabric<br>that makes the room yours.",
    "return_body": "You have seen what form can change. Colour, pattern, texture and character still begin with the fabric.",
